# Keep the build context to what the image actually needs.
#
# The important entry is internal/webui/dist: a developer's local `make scope`
# leaves a built bundle there, and copying it in would put a SECOND, stale set of
# hashed assets next to the one the image builds. Both would be embedded, the
# stale scope.html could win, and the deployed page would load assets that no
# longer exist. Excluding it makes the image's UI come from the image's build,
# always.
internal/webui/dist/*
!internal/webui/dist/.gitkeep

node_modules
site/dist
site/public/moss.wasm
site/public/wasm_exec.js

bin
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.h

# Debug recordings can be hundreds of megabytes and belong to a machine, not an image.
*.mossrec

.git
.github
.continuum
docs
examples
*.md
